  "description": "EXPLORATORY (D-656, program U, U3): the user's journey as one portfolio outcome. Within each of U1's nine configurations across start days: each journey variable's rank correlation with the net cash and with being ahead at months 1 to 3, a standardised regression, moving-block bootstrap intervals, and the accounting split of the net into payouts and fees. Design against luck: the share of the net's variance that is the design. Between the cells of families 1 to 7 and the three rows to beat (hypothetical cells in no row; Lucid cells marked upper bounds): each scorecard measure's rank correlation with P, a standardised regression, intervals from resampling whole families; the frontier and a menu by declared limits. No engine, no variant: a re-reading of files on record; the identities first.",
